  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on a coordinated approach to Grauers gorilla conservation in Eastern DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FFIs DRC programs long-term goal is to enable the effective and sustainable protection of Grauers gorillas by dedicated, empowered local community members. Specific objectives are to: 1) Improve coverage and effectiveness of biomonitoring of Grauers gorilla in REGOLU and REGOMUKI adjacent to Maiko National Park and the Itebero sector of Kahuzi Biega National Park; 2) Develop zoning and demarcate three community forests in REGOLU and REGOMUKI; and 3) Increase awareness and community support for Grauers gorilla conservation.</narrative>
  </description>
